<title>SWEDEN: Swedish consumer prices fall 0.1 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Swedish consumer prices fall 0.1 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish consumer prices fell 0.1 percent in February from January, while the EU-harmonised CPI was unchanged, Statistics Sweden said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>    SWEDISH CONSUMER PRICES     Feb 97     Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	 -0.1	 +0.1	+0.1</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	   -0.4	 -0.1	+1.7</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1980)	 254.2	254.6     255.8</p>
<p>EU-HARMONISED SWEDISH CONSUMER PRICES</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	  0.0	 +0.2     +0.4</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	   +1.1	 +1.2     +1.0</p>
<p>Note - Economists polled by Reuters had expected monthly consumer prices (non-harmonised) to rise by 0.2 percent in February. -- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 10</p>
</text>
